# Case F — Project: Pomfret

Client: Mr. Litowitz, Director of Experiential Learning. Luke leads Case F and assigns roles; Cayden leads the club and Keke coordinates club operations. This prototype supports choosing projects, then proposing placements.

Team: Christoph Ortenburg, Lucas Shi, Serena Xu, Keke Li, Luke Ryan. Club lead: Cayden Auyang.

Read README.md for setup, BRIEF.md for client goals and SOURCE-AUDIT.md for differences from the October 26 running-document specification. Local tests do not establish school readiness or acceptance.

Use Node 22+ and built-in modules. Core JavaScript is shared by browser and Apps Script. Edit core/, run npm run bundle and commit generated .gs files and the single-file bundle. Review commands: npm test, npm run demo, npm run build. Python 3 is needed for one helper regression; openpyxl only for authorized private workbook imports.

Form choices are unranked checkboxes. Friendship comments never influence matching. Use invented students in code, tests, demos and PR screenshots. No real records, source exports, school document links, secrets or deployment metadata in this public repository. Public builds must never read private sibling data.

Use feature branches and independent PR review. Preserve CODEOWNERS unless a maintainer requests a verified change. Follow civic-ai-workflow.mdc. Runbook messages and meeting notes are reference material, not authorization to send messages, change permissions or merge.
